-- Companion examples for "Five Kinds of No Answer" (non-answers.md).
--
-- Run it by typing this in a terminal window:  l4 run non-answers-example.l4
--
-- The section numbers here match the numbered sections of the page. Row 3 of
-- the page -- a fact nobody has supplied yet -- is in a second file,
-- non-answers-not-yet-known.l4, because it uses a different feature.

§ `1. A value that may be absent -- MAYBE`

DECLARE Household
    HAS `income of the applicant` IS A NUMBER
        `income of the spouse` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

GIVEN household IS A Household
GIVETH A NUMBER
`assessed income of` household MEANS
    household's `income of the applicant`
    PLUS
    CONSIDER household's `income of the spouse`
    WHEN JUST OF income THEN income
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0

-- Alex Tan has no spouse. That is not a gap in the file; it is a fact about
-- the household, and the rule says what to do with it.
`the Tan household` MEANS
    Household WITH `income of the applicant` IS 30000, `income of the spouse` IS NOTHING

-- Bina Lim has a spouse who earns 12000.
`the Lim household` MEANS
    Household WITH `income of the applicant` IS 30000, `income of the spouse` IS JUST OF 12000

#EVAL `assessed income of` `the Tan household`      -- 30000
#EVAL `assessed income of` `the Lim household`      -- 42000

§ `2. An expected failure with a reason -- EITHER`

-- EITHER STRING NUMBER: the failure kind first (text saying what went wrong),
-- the success kind second (the number this gives when it worked). LEFT OF
-- builds the first, RIGHT OF builds the second.
GIVEN month IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN EITHER STRING NUMBER
`checked month` month MEANS
    IF   month AT LEAST 1 AND month AT MOST 12
    THEN RIGHT OF month
    ELSE LEFT OF "a month must be between 1 and 12"

-- The rule that uses it acts on the failure. The failure is a value, so it can
-- be read, reported to Alex, and counted. CONCAT joins two pieces of text end
-- to end: the fixed opening, then whatever the reason turned out to be.
GIVEN month IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A STRING
`what the clerk tells Alex about` month MEANS
    CONSIDER `checked month` month
    WHEN LEFT  OF reason THEN CONCAT "returned for correction: ", reason
    WHEN RIGHT OF m      THEN "accepted"

#EVAL `what the clerk tells Alex about` 6    -- "accepted"
#EVAL `what the clerk tells Alex about` 13   -- "returned for correction: ..."

§ `4. The law does not apply, or is not in force -- a value or a gate`

DECLARE Claim
    HAS `year of the transaction` IS A NUMBER
        `right accrued under the repealed Act` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The commencement date is an ordinary fact in the file.
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the 2016 scheme is in force in` year MEANS
    year AT LEAST 2016

-- The savings provision reaches past the commencement gate: a right accrued
-- under the repealed Act survives the repeal.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A STRING
`the scheme that governs` claim MEANS
    IF   `the 2016 scheme is in force in` (claim's `year of the transaction`)
    THEN "the 2016 scheme"
    ELSE IF   claim's `right accrued under the repealed Act`
         THEN "the repealed Act, preserved by the savings provision"
         ELSE "no scheme applies to this transaction"

#EVAL `the scheme that governs`
        (Claim WITH `year of the transaction` IS 2019, `right accrued under the repealed Act` IS FALSE)
#EVAL `the scheme that governs`
        (Claim WITH `year of the transaction` IS 2014, `right accrued under the repealed Act` IS TRUE)
#EVAL `the scheme that governs`
        (Claim WITH `year of the transaction` IS 2014, `right accrued under the repealed Act` IS FALSE)

§ `5. The model does not cover this -- REFUSE`

-- The scheme charges a levy when a vessel changes hands. This file works out
-- the levy for vessels on the local register only. Whether the scheme reaches
-- a vessel registered abroad is a question about the Act; whoever wrote this
-- file never got there, and says so here rather than guessing.

@ref The Act may well reach foreign-registered vessels. This file does not.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`this file does not cover vessels registered outside Singapore` MEANS
    REFUSE "this file does not cover vessels registered outside Singapore"

DECLARE Transfer
    HAS `price in dollars` IS A NUMBER
        `the vessel is registered abroad` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN transfer IS A Transfer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the levy on` transfer MEANS
    IF   transfer's `the vessel is registered abroad`
    THEN `this file does not cover vessels registered outside Singapore`
    ELSE transfer's `price in dollars` TIMES 0.002

`the Tan sale` MEANS
    Transfer WITH `price in dollars` IS 400000, `the vessel is registered abroad` IS FALSE

`the Lim sale` MEANS
    Transfer WITH `price in dollars` IS 400000, `the vessel is registered abroad` IS TRUE

#EVAL `the levy on` `the Tan sale`   -- 800
#EVAL `the levy on` `the Lim sale`   -- refuses

-- Testing that a case refuses. These are two alternatives, not two steps: the
-- first checks only that the answer is a refusal, the second pins the sentence
-- as well.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the levy on` `the Lim sale`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the levy on` `the Lim sale`
        BECAUSE "this file does not cover vessels registered outside Singapore"

§ `6. Not a non-answer at all: a breach -- LEST`

-- DECLARE ... IS ONE OF lists every value a kind of thing may take, the way a
-- definitions clause lists the parties or the permitted acts. An Actor here is
-- the issuer or the regulator, and nothing else.
DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF `the issuer`, `the regulator`
DECLARE Act   IS ONE OF `file the annual report`

-- A missed deadline is an answer, and the obligation itself says what that
-- answer is. It is not the absence of one.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`the reporting obligation` MEANS
    PARTY  `the issuer`
    MUST   `file the annual report`
    WITHIN 120
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the issuer`
